{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "7f3c1a2e-4b58-4e91-9c0d-2a1b3c4d5e6f",
    "name": "Boomi Release Verification",
    "description": "Import this collection plus one of the environments in `postman/` to walk the same Platform API calls `boomi-release-check` makes.\n\n**Mock (no tenant required)**\n1. `python3 tools/mock_boomi_api.py --port 8099`\n2. Import `postman/boomi-release-verification.postman_collection.json`\n3. Import `postman/boomi-mock.postman_environment.json` and select **Boomi Mock (local)**\n4. Run the collection (Collection Runner or Newman)\n\nThe mock answers **202 twice** on `ReleaseIntegrationPackStatus`, then **200 SUCCESS** with packaged versions `6.0`. Account queries page at 2 rows (`queryToken`). Sub-account outcomes:\n\n| Account | Expected |\n| --- | --- |\n| Alpha Logistics | UP_TO_DATE (`6.0`) |\n| Bravo Manufacturing | OUT_OF_DATE (`5.0`) |\n| Charlie Retail | PARTIAL (one `6.0`, one `5.0`) |\n| Delta Health | NOT_DEPLOYED (pack installed, nothing deployed) |\n| Echo Financial | ERROR (HTTP 403) |\n| Foxtrot Energy | UP_TO_DATE (`6.00` matches `6.0`) |\n\n**Live tenant**\nImport `postman/boomi-platform.postman_environment.json`, fill `username` / `apiToken` / `masterAccountId` / `requestId`, and replace the mock sub-account IDs.\n\nAuth is collection-level **Basic** (`{{username}}`:`{{apiToken}}`). Boomi token users look like `BOOMI_TOKEN.you@example.com`.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "basic",
    "basic": [
      {
        "key": "username",
        "value": "{{username}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "password",
        "value": "{{apiToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
